Pretrained models (NOT part of this repository)
-----------------------------------------------
The DDSP instrument runs Magenta's pretrained solo-instrument models (violin, flute, tenor saxophone, trumpet),
exported to .ddspw files by tools/b1/export_weights.py. The weights are not committed to this repository and are not redistributed
with it. scripts/fetch_checkpoints.sh downloads them from Magenta's public storage into models/ (git-ignored), and
the app looks for the exported files in $DDAW_MODELS and ~/Library/Application Support/DDAW/models.
Their terms are unconfirmed: the DDSP repository (Apache-2.0) states no licence for the checkpoints, and the models
were trained on third-party recordings. Before any binary release that bundles weights, confirm the terms with
Magenta/Google (see docs/PLAN.md, risks) or ship without them. Until then, scripts/check_no_weights.sh keeps
them out of git.

DDSP (Magenta), https://github.com/magenta/ddsp   Copyright 2019 Google LLC, Apache License 2.0
  Ported from it (changed, in C++): the harmonic synthesiser, filtered noise, reverb convolution, the F0/loudness
  preprocessing and A-weighted loudness extraction (src/ddsp/, src/dsp/Loudness.*), and the reference scripts in
  tools/b1 and tools/b3 that call the original library to produce test references.

synthyy, Rust/Tauri reference implementation, to be released under the AGPL. DDAW's engine, devices, document model
and fixtures follow its behaviour; the golden fixtures in tests/fixtures/synthyy come from it.

